    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d359">

                <pb facs="0610" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v12p2/pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">S/P–NSC files, lot 61 D 167, NSC 5413/1</note>
                <head>No. 359<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Executive Secretary
                        (Lay) to the National Security Council</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi><lb/>NSC
                        5413/1</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-04-05">April 5, 1954</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">U.S. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Policy Toward The
                        Philippines</hi></p>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>References:</head>
                    <item>A. NSC 5413<anchor n="1" xml:id="d359-f1"/></item>
                    <item>B. NSC Action No. 1084<anchor n="2" xml:id="d359-f2"/></item>
                    <item>C. NSC 84/2<anchor n="3" xml:id="d359-f3"/></item>
                    <item>D. NIE–66–54<anchor n="4" xml:id="d359-f4"/></item>
                </list>
                <p>The National Security Council, the Secretary of the Treasury, Assistant Secretary
                    of Commerce Anderson and the Acting Director, Bureau of the Budget, at the 191st
                    Council meeting on April 1, 1954 adopted the statement of policy on the subject
                    contained in NSC 5413, subject to the changes therein which are set forth in NSC
                    Action No. 1084.</p>
                <pb facs="0611" n="591" xml:id="pg591"/>
                <p>The President on April 1 approved the statement of policy contained in NSC 5413,
                    as amended and adopted by the Council and enclosed herewith; directs its
                    implementation by all appropriate executive departments and agencies of the U.S.
                    Government; and designates the Operations Coordinating Board as the coordinating
                    agency. The Financial Appendix and NSC staff study<anchor n="5" xml:id="d359-f5"
                    /> originally enclosed in NSC 5413 are also transmitted herewith for Council
                    information.</p>
                <p>Accordingly, NSC 84/2 is hereby superseded.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James S. Lay, Jr.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d359-a1.xml" xpointer="d359-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d359-f1" n="1" xml:id="d359-f1-content">
                <p>Dated Mar. 16, NSC 5413, prepared by the NSC Planning Board, was transmitted to
                    the Council on that date for consideration at an early meeting. NSC 5413 did not
                    differ substantially from NSC 5413/1 except as indicated in <ref
                        target="#d360-f2">footnote 2</ref>, below.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d359-f2" n="2" xml:id="d359-f2-content">
                <p>NSC Action No. 1084 was taken at the 191st meeting of the National Security
                    Council on Apr. 1. The changes made in NSC 5413 were minor with the exception of
                    the revision of paragraph 4 to take into account the joint statement of Mar. 22
                    (see <ref target="#d355-f3">footnote 3, Document 355</ref>) and the revision
                    indicated in <ref target="#d360-f6">footnote 6</ref>, below. (611.96/4654)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d359-f3" n="3" xml:id="d359-f3-content">
                <p>For text, see <ref target="frus1950v06#pg_1514"><hi rendition="#italic">Foreign
                            Relations</hi>, 1950, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi>, p.
                        1514</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d359-f4" n="4" xml:id="d359-f4-content">
                <p>See <ref target="#d356">Document 356</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d359-f5" n="5" xml:id="d359-f5-content">
                <p>The staff study is not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
